-8e91-3a139268a2d1" 13194139535929 17592186045443 true] [17592186543812 1074 "To calculate the total circulation of a vector field over the boundary of a region containing holes, we add together the circulations over each *positively oriented* boundary.\n\nRemember that:\n\n- the positive direction is *counterclockwise* for the *outer* curve ${C}_{1}$ (because the region $D$ is always on the left as we traverse ${C}_{1}$ counterclockwise), and\n\n- the positive direction is *clockwise* for the *inner* curves ${C}_{2}$ and ${C}_{3}$ (because the region $D$ is always on the left as we traverse ${C}_{2}$ and ${C}_{3}$ clockwise).\n\nThe diagram below shows the positive orientations of all three curves.\n\n![](images/fa/fa1022d2a1718627898289abdd4d3035a6e06230eea16d0e46832675b2e37def.png)\n\nNotice that the positive orientation of the outer curve ${C}_{1}$ is opposite that of ${C}_{1}$ as stated in the question.\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{∂D}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & =-{∮}_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{∮}_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{∮}_{{C}_{3}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r \\\\  & =-(- \\frac{17}{2})+(- \\frac{19}{3})+\\frac{23}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{-(-51)+(-38)+46}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{59}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535929 17592186045443 true] [17592186543813 1075 #edb/ref 17592186543815 13194139535929 17592186045443 true] [17592186543813 1075 #edb/ref 17592186543820 13194139535929 17592186045443 true] [17592186543813 1075 #edb/ref 17592186543821 13194139535929 17592186045443 true] [17592186543813 1075 #edb/ref 17592186543827 13194139535929 17592186045443 true] [17592186543813 1075 #edb/ref 17592186543838 13194139535929 17592186045443 true] [17592186543813 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139535929 17592186045443 true] [17592186543813 1077 "selection" 13194139535929 17592186045443 true] [17592186543813 1078 #edb/ref 17592186543821 13194139535929 17592186045443 true] [17592186543813 1079 #uuid "4ab8a066-f63f-5bc4-a451-8cc061d5437d" 13194139535929 17592186045443