2186045443 true] [17592186543832 1072 #uuid "ca868da8-dd46-5274-aa8f-98c77655ddad" 13194139535929 17592186045443 true] [17592186543832 1074 "To calculate the total circulation of a vector field over the boundary of a region containing holes, we add together the circulations over each *positively oriented* boundary.\n\nRemember that:\n\n- the positive direction is *counterclockwise* for the *outer* curve ${C}_{1}$ (because the region $D$ is always on the left as we traverse ${C}_{1}$ counterclockwise), and\n\n- the positive direction is *clockwise* for the *inner* curves ${C}_{2}$ and ${C}_{3}$ (because the region $D$ is always on the left as we traverse ${C}_{2}$ and ${C}_{3}$ clockwise).\n\nThe diagram below shows the positive orientations of all three curves.\n\n![](images/fd/fd221ae68fc4983fb0a3f7a745154764e5c0081b2b9b66e7f8ad4a150a8b3bc5.png)\n\nNotice that the positive orientations of the inner curves ${C}_{2}$ and ${C}_{3}$ are opposite to those stated in the question.\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{∂D}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={∮}_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r-{∮}_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r-{∮}_{{C}_{3}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r \\\\  & =(- \\frac{25}{3})-\\frac{16}{3}-\\frac{13}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-50)-32-39}{6} \\\\  & =- \\frac{121}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535929 17592186045443 true] [17592186543833 1080 "- \\frac{47}{6}" 13194139535929 17592186045443 true] [17592186543833 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535929 17592186045443 true] [17592186543833 1083 #uuid "e0d1bfe2-984f-576e-a3ec-0532fcc4e3e1" 13194139535929 17592186045443 true] [17592186543834 1068 #edb/ref 17592186543823 13194139535929 17592186045443 true] [17592186543834 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139535929 17592186045443 true] [17592186543834 1071 "![](images/12/1253965689fbeb233ca3eda553cca8ea8bced9feb81ebc6565c9b65782066b47.png)\n\nSuppose that $F$ is a vector field on ${R}^{2}$ defined over the region $D$ above. Given that \n\n$$\n{∮}_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=\\frac{17}{2},\\,{∮}_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=- \\frac{19}{3},\\,{∮}_{{C}_{3}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=- \\frac{1}{3},\n$$\n\nwhere ${C}_{1}$ and ${C}_{2}$ are oriented counterclockwise and ${C}_{3}$ is oriented clockwise, calculate the value of ${∮}_{∂D}F\\cdot \\text{d}r.$" 13194139535929 17592186045443 true] [17592186543834 1072 #uuid "e8e9f007-9cb8-5437-b13d-dccd4da1a757" 13194139535929 17592186045443 true] [17592186543834 1074 "To calculate the total circulation of a vector field over the boundary of a region containing holes, we add together the circulations over each *positively oriented* boundary.\n\nRemember that:\n\n- the positive direction is *counterclockwise* for the *outer* curve ${C}_{1}$ (because the region $D$ is always on the left as we traverse ${C}_{1}$ counterclockwise), and\n\n- the positive direction is *clockwise* for the *inner* curves ${C}_{2}$ and ${C}_{3}$ (because the region $D$ is always on the left as we traverse ${C}_{2}$ and ${C}_{3}$ clockwise).\n\nThe diagram below shows the positive orientations of all three curves.\n\n![](images/ca/cad0f92fdd888243562619b410a200ca040ca43f83bfd15fb124c8a8ecae4df6.png)\n\nNotice that the positive orientation of the inner curve ${C}_{2}$ is opposite that of ${C}_{2}$ as stated in the question.\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{∂D}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={∮}_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r-{∮}_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{∮}_{{C}_{3}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r \\\\  & =\\frac{17}{2}-(- \\frac{19}{3})+(- \\frac{1}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{51-(-38)+(-2)}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{29}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535929 17592186045443 true] [17592186543835 1080 "- \\frac{89}{6}" 13194139535929 17592186045443 true] [17592186543835 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535929 17592186045443 true] [17592186543835 1083 #uuid "e971687d-bfd0-50d9-822f-623b570efa14" 13194139535929 17592186045443 true] [17592186543836 1068 #edb/ref 17592186543824 13194139535929 17592186045443 true] [17592186543836 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 131